  "question": {
    "text": "If the locus of the point, whose distances from the point $(2,1)$ and $(1,3)$ are in the ratio $5: 4$, is $a x^2+b y^2+c x y+d x+e y+170=0$, then the value of $a^2+2 b+3 c+4 d+e$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "37",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "437",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "-27",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "let $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{x}, \\mathrm{y})$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{(x-2)^2+(y-1)^2}{(x-1)^2+(y-3)^2}=\\frac{25}{16} \\\\\n& 9 x^2+9 y^2+14 x-118 y+170=0 \\\\\n& a^2+2 b+3 c+4 d+e \\\\\n& =81+18+0+56-118 \\\\\n& =155-118 \\\\\n& =37\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}